  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A current carrying rectangular loop <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;is made of uniform wire. The length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. If ammeter current reading changes from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>I</mi></math>, the ratio of magnetic forces per unit length on the wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> due to wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mi>S</mi></math> in the two cases respectively <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo>:</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is:</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8871baaa-4b34-46f3-80f1-a2baff559b41-9895471.PNG\" style=\"width: 306px; height: 130px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "8WtaN",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
